ust protect state that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shares with other handlers.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPRequestHandler"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequestHandler","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPRequestHandler"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPRequestHandler","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttprequesthandler"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse":{"abstract":[{"text":"The answer to a request: a status code, headers and a body. Use the static functions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to create the common responses:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPResponse","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpresponse"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/Body-swift.enum/custom(_:contentType:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A body that a function writes to the connection, for content that is not available as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a whole or too large to hold in memory. Whatever the function writes is sent at once.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Its length is not known, so the body is sent in chunks (","type":"text"},{"code":"Transfer-Encoding: chunked","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the connection can be used for the next request; an HTTP/1.0 client, which does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not know chunks, gets the body up to the end of the connection. If the handler sets a"